; Andree, Programming the IBM 650 (1958), Problem Set 3-11, problem 1(b):
; the same count as count_sequential.650, but seven AUPs spaced round the
; drum, each with its constant 3 words on and its successor 5 past that
; (the book's "5-10 rule", tightened), so both arrive under the heads
; just as they're wanted: six adds per revolution, about 12 times faster.
;
; Try:  r, wait a minute, Enter, then p   (or: ibm650 --run --max-rev 12500)

start 0500

0500  RAU 0503 0507
0507  AUP 0510 0515
0515  AUP 0518 0523
0523  AUP 0526 0531
0531  AUP 0534 0539
0539  AUP 0542 0547
0547  AUP 0501 0507

; the constants
0503  1+
0510  1+
0518  1+
0526  1+
0534  1+
0542  1+
0501  1+
